§ `Importer-view fixture — the hyphenated module`

-- The basename is HYPHENATED on purpose: a hyphenated module name can only
-- be imported backticked (IMPORT `interp-common`), which is how the sibling
-- ground-user.l4 spells it. FIXTURE(d)'s textual importer scan must see that
-- spelling, or this module appears to have no importers at all and
-- `statute` — the §2.5.7 `relevant date` shape, satisfying FIXTURE(a)-(c)
-- module-locally — is dropped from the export.
--
-- `local sample` is the discriminating negative: same module-local shape,
-- but NOT referenced by the importer, so it must still drop. Together the
-- two prove the scan returned real importer names, not a fail-open blanket.

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
statute n MEANS n PLUS 1

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
wrap n MEANS n TIMES 2

GIVETH A NUMBER
`local sample` MEANS 42

#EVAL wrap (statute 1)
#ASSERT wrap `local sample` EQUALS 84
